{"prdMarkdown":"# PRD: Dashboard Loading Skeleton\n\n## Problem\nCurrently, users accessing the internal ops dashboard encounter a blank screen while initial data is being fetched. This lack of visual feedback creates an unpolished experience and leaves users uncertain whether the application is actively loading or unresponsive.\n\n## Goals\n- Provide immediate visual feedback during dashboard data loading by rendering a skeleton placeholder in place of a blank screen.\n- Match the structural layout of the dashboard components to provide a seamless visual progression as real data resolves.\n- Ensure an accessible experience by conveying loading states properly to assistive devices.\n\n## Non-Goals\n- Error states: Handling or rendering failed data requests or offline fallback UI is explicitly out of scope for this phase.\n- Redesigning or modifying the underlying data fetching logic or API client contracts in `src/api/client.js`.\n- Any backend or data model changes.\n\n## User Impact\nUsers will see a polished, structural placeholder matching the layout of the dashboard immediately upon navigation, eliminating perceived lag and reducing uncertainty during initial page load.\n\n## Open Product Questions\n- Should a debounce or minimum display delay (e.g., 200–300ms) be implemented to prevent a jarring visual flicker when data loads quickly or is retrieved from cache?","trdMarkdown":"# TRD: Dashboard Loading Skeleton Implementation\n\n## Architecture Notes\n- **Target Components:** The skeleton layout will be integrated into the dashboard view rendered in `src/App.jsx`, alongside existing navigation components such as `src/components/Header.jsx`.\n- **Data Fetching Integration:** Loading indicators will hook into the fetch state driven by `src/api/client.js` calls within `src/App.jsx`.\n- **Dependencies:** `package.json` currently only lists `react` and `react-router-dom`. No styling library (such as Tailwind CSS) or skeleton component library is installed. The skeleton UI and shimmer animations must either be built using plain CSS/keyframes or introduced via an external package.\n\n## Edge Cases & Dependencies\n- **Styling / Dependencies (`package.json`):** There is currently no pre-installed skeleton library or CSS animation framework. Custom CSS shimmer animations or a dependency evaluation will be required.\n- **Layout Shift / CLS (`src/App.jsx`):** Skeleton placeholder containers, grid units, and paddings must precisely match the final dashboard components to prevent Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS) when data arrives.\n- **Rapid Fetch / Cache Flashing (`src/App.jsx`):** Fast API responses or cached loads may trigger a sub-frame flash of the skeleton UI unless throttled, debounced, or handled with a minimum display delay.\n- **Accessibility:** Screen readers and assistive technology require proper attributes (`aria-busy=\"true\"`, `aria-live=\"polite\"`) to announce the loading state and silence placeholder contents until live content is rendered.\n\n## Engineering Questions\n- Should a third-party skeleton library (such as `react-loading-skeleton`) be added to `package.json`, or should the shimmer animations and skeleton blocks be authored in custom CSS to minimize bundle footprint?\n\n## Estimate\n- **Effort:** 2-3 days under normal conditions, up to 5 days worst case (accounting for bespoke CSS shimmer styling and CLS adjustments)."}